They are summarized below:-
(i) Neither the victim nor the informant would tell even the approximate date and time when the incident first took place at Darbhanga;
(ii) The Investigating Officer did not visit the place of occurrence at Darbhanga;
(iii) The victim was found pregnant for about 5 months when the FIR was lodged.

Therefore, it is obvious that victim was conceived any time before 5 months but the victim failed to state when such incident occurred, by whom such incident occurred and where such incident occurred;
(iv) There is no explanation as to why Chhotu Thakur was relieved of his criminal liability by the informant and her daughter;
(v) when there is specific allegation against the said Chhotu Thakur of committing sexual assault upon the victim Patna High Court CR.
